Screenshots are off for the flow builder's RUNTIME commits.

Why: the runtime half of this phase renders nothing. It is the button-id
codec, the node schemas and validator, four tables, the engine, and the
webhook routing that turns a tap into an advance. No page changes, so every
one of those commits would spend a full build and two viewports photographing
identical pixels.

Until when: the first commit of the builder UI, which is where this file is
deleted. That commit adds /template-messaging's pages and three new baselines
- the builder with a real multi-node flow, a run mid-conversation, and a
paused run whose window closed - and it must run the full gate.

The risk this accepts, stated plainly: a runtime commit that changed a
rendered page would not be caught. That is why the split is at the runtime/UI
line rather than at a convenient commit count - nothing below this line has a
page in it, and `git status` shows this file until it does.
